<content>
  <section><title>Inquiry Project Unit 6 Overview</title>

<title>Part 1: Discovering an Area Model</title>
<para/><item>💬 = turn and talk. Stop and share your responses with your partner. Notice when you have different answers.</item>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
<para/><item>What does the <emphasis>area of a rectangle</emphasis> have to do with <emphasis>multiplication</emphasis>? 💬</item>

<para/><item>Play with <link url="https://phet.colorado.edu/sims/html/area-model-algebra/latest/area-model-algebra_en.html?screens=1,2,3">Area Model Algebra</link> for 5 minutes. Write down two things you notice or have questions about, and one thing a neighbor noticed that is interesting to you. <list type="enumerated">
    <para/><item/>
<para/><item/>
<para/><item/>
</list>

</item>

</list>

<title>Part 2: Understanding an Area Model</title>
<para>Use the Explore Screen to answer the following questions.</para> 

<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
<para/><item>Explain what the red and blue sliders do to the <emphasis>outside</emphasis> of the rectangle.</item> 

<para/><item>Explain what the red and blue sliders do to the <emphasis>inside</emphasis> of the rectangle.</item> 


<para/><item>Describe what changes and what doesn't change when the red and blue sliders are moved. 💬</item>



